The Kern River, originally Rio de San Felipe, later La Porciuncula, is a river in the U.S. state of California, approximately 165 miles (270 km) long. It drains an area of the southern Sierra Nevada mountains northeast of Bakersfield. Fed by snowmelt near Mount Whitney, the river passes through scenic canyons in the mountains and is a popular destination for whitewater rafting and kayaking. It is the southernmost major river system in the Sierra Nevada, and is the only major river in the Sierra that drains in a southerly direction.","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/","review_note":"Wide rapids.","reviewed_on":"2026-10-24","source_text":"Kern River | A drive along the Kern River on route 178 just … | Flickr Explore What’s New Recent Photos Trending Events The Commons Flickr Galleries World Map Camera Finder Flickr Blog ✨ Get Pro Log In Sign Up ✨ Get Pro Log In Explore What’s New Camera Finder Trending Events The Commons Flickr Galleries Flickr Blog About Jobs Blog Advertise Developers Guidelines Help Privacy Legal Terms Cookies English ← → Back to photostream Matthew Dillon RuggyBearLA Kern River A drive along the Kern River on route 178 just to get out of LA for a day. The Kern River, originally Rio de San Felipe, later La Porciuncula, is a river in the U.S. state of California, approximately 165 miles (270 km) long. It drains an area of the southern Sierra Nevada mountains northeast of Bakersfield. Fed by snowmelt near Mount Whitney, the river passes through scenic canyons in the mountains and is a popular destination for whitewater rafting and kayaking. It is the southernmost major river system in the Sierra Nevada, and is the only major river in the Sierra that drains in a southerly direction. Done 515 views 6 faves 0 comments Uploaded on June 30, 2019 Taken on June 23, 2019 Matthew Dillon By: Matthew Dillon Kern River A drive along the Kern River on route 178 just to get out of LA for a day. The Kern River, originally Rio de San Felipe,